  message: "P4 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 9ae4abe13f; owner-requested re-check of open P4 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p4_review_11012026/langs1/). VERDICT: PARTLY-STALE. Reviewed 2026-11-01 on dev 9ae4abe13f (tree-sitter-agda 1.3.3, fx_molon). Part 1 reproduces but is INV-vokir's (P3) mechanism: after a one-constructor data block the next signature splits into two function nodes (foo not emitted), and a following 'data Bool' header is lost too. It does not swallow every later declaration. Part 2 as titled does NOT reproduce: in 4 where-block probes each block nests under its own clause. The F2 correction does reproduce: an empty nested 'module C where' gives an ERROR, enclosing module A is not emitted, and 'run' loses its A chain. agda.py:65-69 repeats the where claim. MECHANISM: tree-sitter-agda 1.3.3 layout errors: a one-entry layout block splits the next declaration (INV-vokir), and an empty nested module body ERRORs the enclosing module. SHARES MECHANISM WITH: INV-vokir. PROPOSED DISPOSITION: split (awaiting owner authorization; status unchanged). PROPOSED REMAINDER TITLE: agda: an empty nested module body (module C where, nothing after) makes tree-sitter-agda ERROR the enclosing module, losing it and later scope chains"  # 92fc
